Here is a simple HTML file containing a website with a "DVD Logo" represented as text that travels in a straight line, bouncing off walls without gravity. I've used JavaScript for the animation logic and CSS to style it cleanly.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>DVD Logo Bounce</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            height: 100vh;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            background-color: #f0f8ff; /* Light blue background */
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        .viewport {
            width: 60%;
            height: 40vh;
            border: 2px solid #333;
            position: relative;
            overflow: hidden; /* Prevent text overflow at edges */
        }
        #dvdlogo {
            position: absolute;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            color: #e63946; /* Red accent for "DVD" feel */
            font-weight: bold;
            text-align: center;
            white-space: nowrap;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="viewport">
        <div id="dvdlogo">DVD Logo</div>
    </div>

    <script>
        const logo = document.getElementById('dvdlogo');
        const viewport = document.querySelector('.viewport');
        let posX = 0;
        let posY = 0;
        const speedX = 4;   // Horizontal velocity (pixels per frame)
        const speedY = 3;   // Vertical velocity (pixels per frame)
        let directionX = 1; // +1 forward, -1 backward on bounce
        let directionY = 1;

        function update() {
            posX += speedX * directionX;
            posY += speedY * directionY;

            // Bounce off walls (no gravity)
            if (posX <= 0 || posX >= viewport.offsetWidth - logo.offsetWidth) {
                directionX *= -1; // Reverse horizontal direction on wall hit
            }
            if (posY <= 0 || posY >= viewport.offsetHeight - logo.offsetHeight) {
                directionY *= -1; // Reverse vertical direction on wall hit
            }

            // Apply position with transform for smooth movement
            logo.style.transform = `translate(calc(${posX}px), ${posY}px)`;

            requestAnimationFrame(update);
        }

        // Start animation loop immediately
        update();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Key Features:
- 📽 **DVD Logo Placeholder**: Uses styled text ("DVD Logo") instead of an image, as requested.
- ⚡ **Bouncing Physics (No Gravity)**: The logo travels in a straight line and reverses direction when hitting any wall (top/bottom/left/right). No gravitational effect is applied—movement remains purely horizontal/vertical with bounce logic.
- 🎨 **Clean Layout**: Light background, bordered viewport to simulate the "play area," and red accent styling for visual identity.
- ✅ **Concise & Functional**: Single HTML file ready to save (e.g., `dvdlogo.html`) and open in any browser. Uses `requestAnimationFrame` for smooth animation.

